# {{ exercise_title }} — agent guide

**This app has two zones. Edit only one of them.**

- **The seam** (edit these to change the exercise): `exercise/schema.py`,
  `exercise/analysis.py`, `exercise/content.md`.
- **The chassis** (identical in every app in this family — do NOT edit per app): the
  backend, the frontend, deployment config, and this `.claude/` guidance.

Adding or changing a measurement field means editing **`exercise/schema.py` only**. The
entry form, the results table, the chart candidates and the export columns are all derived
from that Pydantic model at runtime — they update automatically. You almost never need to
touch the chassis.

Guardrails are enforced in three layers (Addendum A §A4): this file, the
`permissions.deny`/`permissions.ask` lists in `.claude/settings.json`, and the real
enforcement — a `chassis_guard` PreToolUse hook that exits non-zero to block. The three name
the same protected set.

