## Editable with confirmation (sensitive, but sometimes legitimately changed)

- `frontend/src/theme.css` — the CPDSE identity. Only the palette tokens live here; never add
  a hex value elsewhere, and never invent an error red/amber (the palette has none).
- `.adalab/local_container_demo.json` — deploy resources for this app.
- `pyproject.toml`, `frontend/package.json`, and dependency-add commands — for adding a
  library your analysis needs.

The always-writable zone is the exercise seam: `exercise/**`.

## You want to… → edit

- Add / change / remove a measurement field → `exercise/schema.py`
- Change field units, ranges, or help text → `exercise/schema.py` (in the `Field(...)`)
- Add a dropdown / date / notes field → `exercise/schema.py` (`Literal[...]`, `date`, `str | None`)
- Add exercise-specific statistics on the Results page → `exercise/analysis.py` (`summarize(df)`)
- Change the Home-page instructions → `exercise/content.md`

The form, table, charts and export **follow the schema** — do not hand-edit them.

## How the pieces fit (so you don't reinvent them)

- Persistence is **append-only** with cohort semantics. Students never edit or delete;
  a correction *supersedes*. "Reset for a new class" = an admin *closes* the cohort and
  *opens* a new one. Nothing is ever deleted. Do not invent your own storage — see
  `.claude/skills/lab-exercise-app/references/data-model.md`.
- Data lives on a mounted AdaLab Shared Volume at `$DATA_DIR` (default `/asv-mnt/lab-data`).
  The app **fails loud** if that volume isn't mounted/writable — never point `DATA_DIR` at a
  container-local path to "fix" a startup error; that silently loses a year of data.
- The measurement contract lives in `exercise/schema.py` as a single Pydantic model named
  `Measurement`. Keep that name.

## Conventions

Style and component rules are in `.claude/rules/`. Use the **`lab-exercise-app`** skill for
any request to adapt the app, and `/new-exercise-field` to add a field interactively.
